1
00:01:45,479 --> 00:01:47,440
Why are you tapping on it?

2
00:01:48,445 --> 00:01:52,738
Doing this tells me where the wood is rotten or eaten by bugs.

3
00:01:52,856 --> 00:01:53,795
Bugs?

4
00:01:54,249 --> 00:01:55,760
Wood-eating bugs.

5
00:02:02,139 --> 00:02:04,191
Oops, found one.

6
00:02:05,926 --> 00:02:07,246
Look here.

7
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,100
Ugh, gross!

8
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:13,480
All right, then let's burn this piece.

9
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:18,245
What happens if we just leave it?

10
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:22,600
When heavy rain fills the pond, the sluice gate will break.

11
00:02:23,174 --> 00:02:25,400
Hmm, why would it break?

12
00:02:25,440 --> 00:02:27,320
From the water pressure.

13
00:02:27,620 --> 00:02:32,180
Pressure is incredible. But just one tiny hole should be fine, right?

14
00:02:32,454 --> 00:02:37,320
No, no. As the saying goes, even a massive levee can collapse from a single ant hole.

15
00:02:37,765 --> 00:02:38,897
What does that mean?

16
00:02:39,330 --> 00:02:45,400
It means even a sturdy dike can be destroyed starting from one little ant hole.

17
00:03:05,430 --> 00:03:07,860
Always be careful, even with little things.

18
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:11,280
That's terrible. Then everything would be flooded!

19
00:03:12,114 --> 00:03:14,220
Indeed. And that's not all.

20
00:03:14,445 --> 00:03:20,420
If the reservoir empties, crops won't grow, and we won't have drinking water either.

21
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:23,920
Oh no, that's awful! I'll help you too.

22
00:03:25,783 --> 00:03:26,298
Here.

23
00:03:27,015 --> 00:03:30,340
Thank you. You're such a kind boy.

24
00:03:36,410 --> 00:03:38,254
Hey Mokku!

25
00:03:38,738 --> 00:03:40,332
Mokku!

26
00:03:40,816 --> 00:03:42,941
Over here! Over here!

27
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:45,560
Why are you calling Mokku?

28
00:03:46,165 --> 00:03:49,020
You don't get it? We're gonna use him.

29
00:03:49,364 --> 00:03:50,489
Use him how?

30
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:52,060
The water's still cold, right?

31
00:03:52,420 --> 00:03:56,074
So we put Mokku in the water to flush out the fish.

32
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:58,835
Oh, I see. Good idea.

33
00:03:59,255 --> 00:04:03,114
We're catching fish! It's fun! Come over here!

34
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:06,778
Fish? What should I do?

35
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:08,905
I'm going!

36
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:11,898
Hey, Mokku!

37
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:14,795
Wait! I'm coming!

38
00:04:15,100 --> 00:04:16,441
Hopeless boy.

39
00:04:17,473 --> 00:04:19,213
He's only interested in playing.

40
00:04:23,098 --> 00:04:25,646
All right, do your best! Did it slip away?

41
00:04:28,059 --> 00:04:30,238
Go! Get 'em, get 'em, get 'em!

42
00:04:31,723 --> 00:04:33,301
Get 'em, get 'em!

43
00:04:51,117 --> 00:04:52,594
We did it!

44
00:05:01,022 --> 00:05:03,875
Phew, I'm exhausted! Man, look, that's carp!

45
00:05:03,899 --> 00:05:05,679
The smell is incredible. 

46
00:05:05,977 --> 00:05:08,257
Look how plump it is! Let's cook those bad boys up!

47
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:12,250
Honestly, my mouth is drooling like crazy. I wonder why...

48
00:05:12,757 --> 00:05:15,160
A fresh carp washed-sashimi, ready to serve, baby!

49
00:05:15,236 --> 00:05:17,140
Whoa, now you're talking, Boss!

50
00:05:17,164 --> 00:05:20,273
You sure know your stuff when it comes to good snacks, so no wonder you know your way around cooking!

51
00:05:20,297 --> 00:05:23,580
A bit of fresh carp sashimi... I can't resist! I wonder why...

52
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:31,984
Idiot! I'm starving! That lunch of yours didn't fill me up at all! Look at this!

53
00:05:33,826 --> 00:05:35,760
Huh? I'm sorry, boss.

54
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:37,920
All right, go swipe that carp!

55
00:05:37,979 --> 00:05:41,743
W-What? No, I can't! At night maybe, but in broad daylight...

56
00:05:43,429 --> 00:05:48,560
You slow-witted fool. You've got a weasel's last trick—a real good stinker—don't you?

57
00:05:48,855 --> 00:05:53,500
But, Boss, that's what you use when you're running away. I wonder why.

58
00:05:54,423 --> 00:05:56,688
What do you mean "I wonder why"?! You distract them with a stink...

59
00:05:56,712 --> 00:05:59,147
...powerful enough to rip their nose off, and that's your chance!

60
00:05:59,315 --> 00:06:01,250
Hey, brilliant!

61
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,560
Ready?

62
00:06:18,529 --> 00:06:19,175
Stand by!

63
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:22,480
Ready to go?

64
00:06:23,415 --> 00:06:26,140
Gotta go! Gotta go! Gotta go!

65
00:06:32,909 --> 00:06:33,807
He did it!

66
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:58,840
Boss, it's the wind's fault! It's the wind!

67
00:06:58,940 --> 00:07:00,000
I wonder why.

68
00:07:02,049 --> 00:07:03,336
Swish, swish, swish!

69
00:07:04,431 --> 00:07:05,795
Get outta here! Shoo!

70
00:07:14,850 --> 00:07:16,400
It came off!

71
00:07:17,105 --> 00:07:18,883
It's detached!

72
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,540
What's this? A wood bug?

73
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,480
Huh? It looks just like the bugs at the sluice gate!

74
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,240
I see, it washed down here.

75
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,817
Unbelievable, trying to eat my foot.

76
00:07:46,501 --> 00:07:50,220
Did the bugs eat away at it and mess up the measurements where his knee moves?

77
00:07:50,321 --> 00:07:51,602
Could have.

78
00:08:00,992 --> 00:08:03,076
Can you even walk like that?!

79
00:08:03,100 --> 00:08:04,330
I think so, but...

80
00:08:09,131 --> 00:08:10,210
This is weird...

81
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:20,116
He's broken! He's broken!

82
00:08:21,590 --> 00:08:23,178
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go home!

83
00:08:23,329 --> 00:08:23,894


84
00:08:24,270 --> 00:08:25,809
Damn that Franco!

85
00:08:27,350 --> 00:08:29,120
Grandpa will make me a new one!

86
00:08:56,303 --> 00:08:58,478
All done. Here is your new leg.

87
00:08:58,503 --> 00:08:59,886
Cool!

88
00:09:00,221 --> 00:09:02,512
It's the exact same size as the old one.

89
00:09:03,269 --> 00:09:04,985
Here, let me attach it for you.

90
00:09:08,165 --> 00:09:11,946
Well, no one will laugh at you now. Try walking.

91
00:09:12,298 --> 00:09:13,540
Thank you, Grandpa.

92
00:09:17,510 --> 00:09:18,469
What is the matter?

93
00:09:20,129 --> 00:09:21,280
I tripped.

94
00:09:27,749 --> 00:09:28,980
Your leg won't move.

95
00:09:39,905 --> 00:09:40,905
Mokku!

96
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,240
Grandpa, why did you make me a leg like this?!

97
00:09:47,810 --> 00:09:50,065
I want a leg that moves like before!

98
00:09:50,595 --> 00:09:52,740
B-But even if you say that...

99
00:09:52,939 --> 00:09:56,003
Grandpa has no idea why it won't move either...

100
00:10:36,590 --> 00:10:37,840
How nice...

101
00:10:38,139 --> 00:10:40,960
When everyone else plays in the river, they don't get wood bugs...

102
00:10:41,309 --> 00:10:44,452
Even if they get muddy, they're fine once they wash off!

103
00:10:45,919 --> 00:10:48,031
And yet, I'm... (sobbing)

104
00:10:52,289 --> 00:10:57,867
I hate this... I hate it! I don't want to be a puppet anymore!

105
00:11:02,319 --> 00:11:03,790
M-Mokku...

106
00:11:26,002 --> 00:11:30,620
Don't you get it? Even if it's made from fine oak, it won't move.

107
00:11:34,569 --> 00:11:37,315
Not without the Oak Tree Fairy's power.

108
00:11:45,604 --> 00:11:47,222
Aaah... I'm so hungry!

109
00:11:47,247 --> 00:11:50,605
I've got to eat somehow! I wonder why.

110
00:11:50,629 --> 00:11:56,120
Man, I want to eat carp. I've gotta eat carp somehow. I want to eat carp.

111
00:11:57,135 --> 00:11:59,485
Wait! I've got a great idea!

112
00:12:00,274 --> 00:12:02,193
Jackpot! Time to eat!

113
00:12:02,455 --> 00:12:05,073
Huh? A master who can make legs that move?

114
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:07,480
Shh! Keep your voice down!

115
00:12:07,595 --> 00:12:10,600
That's right! There's a master leg-maker around!

116
00:12:10,875 --> 00:12:12,696
W-Where is this master?

117
00:12:13,149 --> 00:12:14,524
You want us to tell you?

118
00:12:14,749 --> 00:12:15,820
Please!

119
00:12:17,790 --> 00:12:20,435
I could tell you, but not for free!

120
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,781
Yeah!

121
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:24,440
What do you mean? What should I do?

122
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:29,080
Oh, nothing much. Just lend us a hand for a bit. Simple as that.

123
00:12:52,059 --> 00:12:53,720
Even this is better than not being able to move.

124
00:12:56,689 --> 00:12:58,640
Mokku, what are you doing?

125
00:12:59,425 --> 00:13:00,425
I'm leaving.

126
00:13:02,170 --> 00:13:03,360
Leaving? Where to?

127
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:05,880
Leave me alone. What does it matter where?

128
00:13:19,359 --> 00:13:21,680
Fine. If you want to know that badly, I'll tell you.

129
00:13:22,309 --> 00:13:28,460
I'm going to a master puppet maker who's way, way better than Grandpa, to have him make me a persimmon!

130
00:13:28,665 --> 00:13:29,960
Much better?

131
00:13:30,540 --> 00:13:31,060
That's right.

132
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:33,380
There's no master like that.

133
00:13:34,300 --> 00:13:34,800
Yes, there is!

134
00:13:35,145 --> 00:13:38,860
Nobody anywhere can make a puppet that moves like a real human.

135
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:41,940
Yes, there is! I heard all about him!

136
00:13:42,735 --> 00:13:43,800
No, there isn't.

137
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:50,540
Goodbye. Good night!

138
00:13:50,939 --> 00:13:51,939
Mokku!

139
00:14:18,020 --> 00:14:21,040
Hmm, having legs that won't move must be tough.

140
00:14:21,310 --> 00:14:23,580
Come on, tell me. What do you want me to do?

141
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:29,820
It's simple, really. Just catch two or three fish from this reservoir for me.

142
00:14:30,075 --> 00:14:34,020
Catch them? How, without any tools?

143
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:43,960
It's a piece of cake. Look, we just open this floodgate and drain the water. Then you can just grab 'em with your bare hands without any gear.

144
00:14:44,109 --> 00:14:48,080
All right, I'll try. But in return, once you catch the fish, you have to...

145
00:14:48,539 --> 00:14:50,000
Yeah, I'll push you!

146
00:14:53,170 --> 00:14:58,320
Good boy, good boy. We don't have to lift a finger and we can eat all we want, that's how it is.

147
00:14:59,020 --> 00:15:03,860
As expected of you, Brother, your mind is so sharp. I wonder why that is.

148
00:15:08,640 --> 00:15:09,640
(Sound of running water)

149
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,220
Hey, Mokku!

150
00:15:13,289 --> 00:15:17,320
If you do that, the water will rush out and the whole town will be in big trouble!

151
00:15:18,335 --> 00:15:19,680
What, you again?!

152
00:15:20,125 --> 00:15:23,260
Stop it, Mokku! Are you trying to flood the whole town?!

153
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:26,880
Shut up! I want legs! Legs that move!

154
00:15:28,290 --> 00:15:29,290
(Sound of water splashing)

155
00:15:30,630 --> 00:15:32,400
Hey, hurry it up!

156
00:15:32,645 --> 00:15:35,920
If the handle won't work, why not try smashing it with a rock?

157
00:15:52,824 --> 00:15:56,180
I'm starving... I want food...

158
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:58,520
Here?

159
00:16:01,045 --> 00:16:03,140
Brother, it's raining.

160
00:16:03,980 --> 00:16:05,060
Shall we go?

161
00:16:06,819 --> 00:16:07,819
Where are you going?

162
00:16:08,859 --> 00:16:11,420
To take shelter from the rain. I hate getting wet.

163
00:16:11,760 --> 00:16:13,240
Please tell me if you're leaving.

164
00:16:13,829 --> 00:16:16,100
You bastard! Are you trying not to let me eat?!

165
00:16:30,329 --> 00:16:34,060
That Kenken... next time I see him, he won't get off easy!

166
00:16:39,419 --> 00:16:43,500
The ants have it nice. Under the big tree, not having to worry about the rain.

167
00:16:59,649 --> 00:17:03,940
Please rest a little...

168
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:14,300
Please rest a little...

169
00:17:18,160 --> 00:17:26,160
Please rest a little...

170
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:35,760
There's so much water...

171
00:17:46,009 --> 00:17:51,800
That's where I slammed into it...

172
00:17:55,120 --> 00:18:03,120
It won't stop...

173
00:18:03,419 --> 00:18:07,200
As they say, even a massive dike can collapse from a single ant hole.

174
00:18:07,584 --> 00:18:12,160
Even a sturdy dike can be destroyed by one tiny ant hole!

175
00:18:15,249 --> 00:18:16,249
Grandpa!

176
00:18:23,109 --> 00:18:26,980
What are you dawdling for?! Hurry up and plug the leak!

177
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:28,460
H-How?

178
00:18:28,934 --> 00:18:30,340
Stuff it with wood!

179
00:18:30,514 --> 00:18:32,100
Wood? There isn't any wood around here!

180
00:18:32,409 --> 00:18:34,220
Yes there is! You're made of wood!

181
00:18:34,514 --> 00:18:38,060
M-Me? You're telling me to use my own body to stop the water?

182
00:18:38,504 --> 00:18:40,220
There's no other way!

183
00:18:40,300 --> 00:18:41,320
No! I don't want to!

184
00:18:48,500 --> 00:18:49,500
There!

185
00:18:51,899 --> 00:18:55,420
What are you messing around for?! Hurry, or the floodgate will break!

186
00:18:56,054 --> 00:18:59,620
No way! If I lose these arms and legs, there are no replacements!

187
00:18:59,725 --> 00:19:02,620
Fine! Then let the whole town drown in water!

188
00:19:02,964 --> 00:19:04,660
Grandpa will just drown and die, too!

189
00:20:28,419 --> 00:20:31,320
Thank goodness, it held.

190
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:32,960
Hm?

191
00:20:35,899 --> 00:20:37,120
Mokku!

192
00:20:39,529 --> 00:20:43,840
Mokku...

193
00:20:48,149 --> 00:20:50,180
Mokku, you...

194
00:20:51,220 --> 00:20:52,220
Mokku...

195
00:20:53,229 --> 00:20:57,840
You drove your own body into it for me...?

196
00:21:11,929 --> 00:21:12,980
Well, Grandpa.

197
00:21:13,294 --> 00:21:15,720
I'm going to go deliver the order.

198
00:21:55,429 --> 00:21:56,960
You are...

199
00:21:57,409 --> 00:22:04,180
Mokku, I saw everything. Your noble deed. You did well to save the townspeople.

200
00:22:05,694 --> 00:22:16,500
You were magnificent. Truly magnificent. I have come to give you life once again. [Music]

201
00:22:19,265 --> 00:22:20,265
I can move!

202
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:28,620
Please, wait! How was I restored?

203
00:22:30,094 --> 00:22:36,900
You sacrificed your precious limbs to save others. Compassion for people...

204
00:22:37,449 --> 00:22:41,360
...that is the heart known as love. Your love...

205
00:22:42,129 --> 00:22:45,520
...has given you life. / My love did?

206
00:22:57,185 --> 00:23:01,400
Come on! Hey, this is dangerous!

207
00:23:02,580 --> 00:23:05,180
Whaaat?! A fork?!

208
00:23:06,389 --> 00:23:12,220
Look out if you're not paying attention! We're in the middle of a match! Hey, Mokku!

209
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:13,640
Hurry!

210
00:23:13,660 --> 00:23:14,300
Wait!

211
00:23:14,360 --> 00:23:15,400
Get 'em!

212
00:23:15,839 --> 00:23:16,860
Nice going, Mokku!

213
00:23:24,049 --> 00:23:25,320
Get 'em!

214
00:23:33,969 --> 00:23:39,040
Mokku becomes friends with Chikaro, a monkey who can speak just like a human.

215
00:23:40,029 --> 00:23:46,940
Learning that Chikaro lives in a wealthy mansion, Kenken and the others threaten Mokku to make him bring them food.

216
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:55,740
However, when Mokku is caught stealing the food, he ends up chained up along with Chikaro, who is about to be sold to a circus.

217
00:23:56,685 --> 00:23:58,980
Don't miss next week's Kashi no Ki Mokku!

